From b6ad7f40de3303eec4640e8f1eed6415dd3ab9e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:31:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add refund policy + refund-safe instructor earnings hold
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New /refund-policy.html: 14-day refund window, blocked once >20% of a
  course is completed (both configurable via env), linked from the
  homepage footer, Privacy Policy and Instructor Policy.
- POST /api/orders/:id/refund-request now enforces that window/progress
  rule server-side instead of accepting any paid order unconditionally;
  GET /api/orders/mine annotates each order with refundEligible/reason so
  the UI can show or hide the action without guessing.
- Added a "Request refund" button to Purchase History (public/payments.js)
  — there was previously no student-facing way to call the existing
  refund-request endpoint at all.
- instructor_earnings rows now start 'pending' with an available_at a few
  days past the refund window (EARNINGS_HOLD_DAYS), instead of 'available'
  the instant an order is paid, so a payout can never be approved while
  the order could still be refunded out from under it. Every query that
  sums "available" earnings (/api/instructor/earnings, /api/admin/payouts,
  /api/admin/payouts/approve, the admin user profile) treats a matured
  pending row as available on its own; the daily cron
  (api/cron/maintenance.js) also flips the stored status once matured, so
  what's displayed stays accurate.
- Instructor Payouts page explains the hold and shows when pending funds
  clear; checkout and Purchase History both surface the policy in plain
  language.

New env vars (api/index.js, .env.example): REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS (14),
REFUND_MAX_PROGRESS_PERCENT (20), EARNINGS_HOLD_DAYS (17).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
